# skills.sh universal install mirror (regenerable via 'npx skills add'); CCv3 vendors real dirs in .claude/skills/
.agents/

# Codex CLI local mirror of the hook/skill/agent library (regenerable; analogous to .agents/ above)
.codex/
# Codex worker isolated git worktrees (throwaway per-run; created by /codex --implement)
.codex-worktrees/

# Grok worker isolated git worktrees (throwaway per-run; created by /grok --implement).
# Both worktree dirs live OUTSIDE the repo as siblings; these entries are defensive.
.grok-worktrees/

# Tri-model workroom runtime rooms (per-feature runtime churn; auto-commit hooks must
# never sweep these in). PROTOCOL.md and templates/ under .workroom/ ARE committed.
# Share a specific contract deliberately via: git add -f .workroom/rooms/<id>/CONTRACT.md
.workroom/rooms/
# Active-room pointer (machine-local runtime state)
.workroom/active-room

# codegraph per-project index DB (derived/disposable; regenerated by `codegraph index`/`sync`)
.codegraph/

# Large local binaries / profilers (kept on disk, not in the repo)
tools/PerfView.exe
tools/*.exe

# claude-for-sales packaged-skill build artifacts (SKILL.md is the source; zip is a repackage)
docs/claude-for-sales/skills/**/*.zip

# project-cards sweep + shared hub-page write locks (machine-local transient runtime state)
scripts/project-cards/.sweep.lock
scripts/project-cards/.hub.lock

# MCP tool-schema catalog dumps (local reference; regenerated per MCP server)
mcps/

# Local DB backups (pre-migration safety dumps) - never commit
#
# `.backups/` alone matched NOTHING: the real directory is `.claude/backups/`, so the
# dumps and the settings snapshots below were still fully committable. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v` -- all four paths came back EXPOSED. Keeping the original
# pattern as well, since a top-level `.backups/` may exist on another machine.
.backups/
.claude/backups/

# settings.json snapshots taken around risky edits. These are NOT harmless copies --
# they embed a literal DATABASE_URL with credentials, so an accidental `git add -A`
# would commit a secret. That is not hypothetical on this branch: one session's commit
# has already swept up another session's staged files.
.claude/settings.json.bak-*
# Rendered per machine. The template is the committed source.
.claude/settings.json

# SpecStory local conversation-history mirror (500+ personal session transcripts)
.specstory/

# Machine-local editor config
.vscode/

# Machine-local Claude Code config. Untracked 2026-07-28: it had been committed to a
# pushed repo carrying 21 permission grants (including Bash(powershell:*) and
# Bash(node:*)), zero deny entries, and enableAllProjectMcpServers - while
# .claude/rules/sync-known-gaps.md declares this file "NEVER sync". No secrets in it,
# so no rotation was needed; the file itself is untouched on disk.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Independent projects parked inside this repo. sites/fastmcp-v3 is its OWN git
# repo (main @ e6c2ae9, clean, no remote), so committing it here would create an
# embedded-repo gitlink rather than tracking the files. It is not CCv3 content.
# NOTE: it has no remote, so its only copy is this working tree -- give it one.
sites/

# One-off design captures from the sites/fastmcp-v3 build (artifacts, not content)
fastmcp-*.png

# Stray nested .claude/ trees. Something writes .claude/logs/intel-bus.jsonl
# RELATIVE TO ITS CWD, so running from .claude/hooks/ or .claude/hooks/src/
# creates .claude/hooks/.claude/logs/ and .claude/hooks/src/.claude/logs/.
# Runtime logs, never content. Ignored rather than deleted so the writer's
# cwd bug stays visible on disk; the real fix is an absolute path in the writer.
.claude/**/.claude/

# Generated lane board. `render-board.mjs` defaults its output here, and the page
# is a BUILD ARTIFACT of the generator plus the live database -- committing a 97KB
# snapshot of it would create exactly the second source of truth the generated
# board exists to eliminate. The generator is the tracked source; see
# .claude/artifacts.json -> agentic-os-lane-board.
/lane-board.html

# Session scratch that research and QA runs leave in the repo root (Opus 5.5 eval, P39).
# Agents should write these to the session scratchpad instead.
/.tmp_research*
/*.png

# Skill eval fixtures are test inputs, not runtime output: track them even when a
# generic rule above (*.log, plans/) matches. Folders first: git cannot re-include a
# file inside an excluded folder.
!.claude/skills/**/evals/files/**/
!.claude/skills/**/evals/files/**

# recall eval full report (regenerated each run; numbers live in the .md and the baseline)
opc/tests/recall_eval_v2_report.json

# rule-router weekly report (regenerated by the scheduled audit)
docs/self-improvement/audits/rule-router-*.md
